<section class="legal-content">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="legal-body">

      <h2>1. Information We Collect</h2>
      <p>We collect information you give us directly and data generated automatically when you use StickVault.</p>

      <h3>Information you provide</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Email address</strong> — when you subscribe to our newsletter or download a free guide via any email capture form on the site.</li>
        <li><strong>Purchase information</strong> — when you buy a digital product, Stripe processes your payment. We receive a confirmation that the transaction completed but we do not store credit card numbers, billing addresses, or full payment details.</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Information collected automatically</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Analytics data</strong> — page views, referrer URLs, session identifiers, and browser/device information collected through our in-house analytics system and, when enabled, Google Analytics 4.</li>
        <li><strong>Affiliate click data</strong> — when you click an affiliate link, we log the click event (timestamp, destination, page source) to track commission activity and measure content performance.</li>
        <li><strong>Cookies</strong> — see our <a href="/cookie-policy" class="legal-link">Cookie Policy</a> for details on what cookies we use and why.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>2. How We Use Your Information</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Email marketing</strong> — we send newsletters, new content announcements, and product updates to subscribers who opted in. Every email includes a one-click unsubscribe link.</li>
        <li><strong>Analytics</strong> — to understand which content resonates, improve site performance, and make better editorial decisions.</li>
        <li><strong>Affiliate tracking</strong> — to attribute commissions correctly and measure the effectiveness of product recommendations.</li>
        <li><strong>Fraud prevention</strong> — Stripe and our payment infrastructure use transaction data to detect and prevent fraudulent purchases.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>3. Third-Party Services</h2>
      <p>We use the following third-party services that may receive or process your data:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Stripe</strong> — payment processing for digital product purchases. <a href="https://stripe.com/privacy" class="legal-link" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Stripe Privacy Policy</a></li>
        <li><strong>Google Analytics</strong> — website traffic analytics (when active). <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" class="legal-link" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Privacy Policy</a></li>
        <li><strong>Pinterest</strong> — we use Pinterest-compatible metadata on our pages. If you engage with Pinterest save buttons, Pinterest's privacy policy applies. <a href="https://policy.pinterest.com/en/privacy-policy" class="legal-link" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Pinterest Privacy Policy</a></li>
        <li><strong>Email service provider</strong> — we use a transactional email platform to deliver newsletters. Subscriber email addresses are stored on that platform's infrastructure in accordance with their privacy terms.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>We do not sell or rent your personal information to third parties.</p>

      <h2>4. Data Retention</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Email subscribers</strong> — retained until you unsubscribe. After unsubscribing, your email is removed from active lists within 30 days.</li>
        <li><strong>Analytics data</strong> — retained for up to 26 months for trend analysis, then aggregated or deleted.</li>
        <li><strong>Purchase records</strong> — retained for 7 years as required for tax and accounting compliance.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>5. Your Rights</h2>
      <p>You have the right to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Unsubscribe</strong> — use the unsubscribe link in any email or contact us at <a href="mailto:hello@stickvault.com" class="legal-link">hello@stickvault.com</a></li>
        <li><strong>Access your data</strong> — request a copy of the personal information we hold about you</li>
        <li><strong>Delete your data</strong> — request deletion of your personal information from our systems</li>
        <li><strong>Correct your data</strong> — request correction of inaccurate information</li>
      </ul>
      <p>To exercise any of these rights, email <a href="mailto:hello@stickvault.com" class="legal-link">hello@stickvault.com</a> with your request. We will respond within 30 days.</p>

      <h2>6. Security</h2>
      <p>We use industry-standard security measures including HTTPS encryption for all data in transit. Payment data is handled exclusively by Stripe, which is PCI DSS compliant. No system is perfectly secure — if you have concerns about a specific security issue, contact us immediately.</p>

      <h2>7. Children's Privacy</h2>
      <p>StickVault is not directed at children under 13. We do not knowingly collect personal information from children. If we learn we have collected data from a child under 13, we will delete it promptly.</p>

      <h2>8. Changes to This Policy</h2>
      <p>We may update this privacy policy from time to time. We will update the "Last updated" date at the top of this page when we do. Continued use of the site after changes constitutes acceptance of the updated policy.</p>

      <h2>9. Contact</h2>
      <p>Questions about this privacy policy? Email <a href="mailto:hello@stickvault.com" class="legal-link">hello@stickvault.com</a></p>

